---
layout: layouts/base.njk
title: Bonfire — Mosaic
description: "A community space that's yours to keep. We co-design it around how your community actually works, and you own it outright: forkable, exportable, impossible to take away."
---
{% set eyebrow = "flex items-center gap-3 font-smono text-[1rem] font-bold tracking-[.18em]" %}
{% set display = "mt-4 font-disp font-[560] text-[clamp(1.6rem,3vw,2.35rem)] leading-[1.06] tracking-[-.02em] text-balance [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]" %}
{% set bodyp = "mt-3.5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[42rem]" %}
{% set btnfire = "btn h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full border-0 px-[1.4rem] py-[.85rem] font-smono text-[.78rem] font-bold tracking-[.05em] text-[#221302] bg-gradient-to-br from-spark via-flame to-ember hover:from-spark hover:via-flame hover:to-ember shadow-[0_6px_26px_-8px_rgba(232,145,43,.55)]" %}
{% set btnline = "btn btn-ghost h-auto min-h-0 rounded-full px-[1.4rem] py-[.85rem] font-smono text-[.78rem] font-bold tracking-[.05em] text-ink border border-ink/15 bg-ink/[0.03] hover:border-flame hover:text-spark hover:bg-ink/[0.03]" %}
{% set phin = "flex items-center justify-center text-center font-smono text-[.72rem] text-ink-3 p-[18px] leading-[1.6] bg-[repeating-linear-gradient(135deg,transparent_0_22px,rgba(242,236,219,.022)_22px_44px)] [&_.tag]:text-flame [&_.tag]:block [&_.tag]:mb-1" %}

<div class="relative overflow-x-clip bg-night text-ink font-body leading-[1.55] antialiased selection:bg-ember selection:text-[#160c02]">
  <div class="v2-ambient" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="relative z-[1]">

    {# ===== hero — the ownership promise ===== #}
    <header class="pt-[34px] pb-14">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">Bonfire Mosaic</p>
      <h1 class="mt-[18px] font-disp font-semibold text-[clamp(2rem,4.8vw,3.6rem)] leading-[1.04] text-balance max-w-[15ch] [font-variation-settings:'opsz'_96]">A community space that's <span class="fire-text">yours to keep.</span></h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[1.12rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[54ch]">Most communities online live on borrowed land: a platform that owns your members, sets the rules, raises the price, and can lock the doors whenever it likes. <b class="text-ink font-semibold">Mosaic is the opposite.</b> We co-design a space around how your community works, and you own it outright: forkable, exportable, impossible to take away.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-3 mt-[26px]">
        <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Book a call</a>
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="#built">See what we've built</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-6 font-smono text-[.72rem] text-ink-3 max-w-[62ch] leading-[1.7]">◼ We work closely with a handful of communities a year. We build the space with you and hand it over as yours.</p>

      {# hero visual — the finished, owned space #}
      <figure class="mt-9 m-0">
        <img class="rounded-xl border border-ink/15 aspect-[16/8] w-full object-cover" src="/img/jacobin/ghostbonfire.png" alt="A community's own space on Bonfire, in their own brand and language, recognisably theirs" loading="lazy">
      </figure>
    </div></header>

    {# ===== rented vs owned — the core contrast ===== #}
    <section class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">Rented vs. owned</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[24ch]">Most communities online <span class="font-light">don't belong to the community.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">There are only two ways to run a community space. The difference comes down to who holds the keys. <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="/compare">See how the options stack up →</a></p>

      {% set liw = "grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-3.5" %}
      {% set libh = "font-disp font-semibold block mb-[3px] text-[.98rem]" %}
      {% set libt = "text-ink-2 text-[.92rem] leading-[1.55]" %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[821px]:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-[30px]">

        {# rented — muted, cautionary #}
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-ink/15 bg-night-2 px-[26px] py-7">
          <span class="font-smono text-[.68rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-ink-3">Renting space on a platform</span>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[18px] mt-[18px]">
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-3/70 [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }} text-ink-2">You look like everyone else</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Same templates, same layout, same defaults. A client once told us every community on these tools ends up looking identical.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-3/70 [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }} text-ink-2">You live on their terms</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Prices, rules and features change without asking you. You adapt, or you leave and lose everything.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-3/70 [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }} text-ink-2">It can disappear</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Get cancelled, acquired or shut down, and your community goes with it. You were only ever a tenant.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-ink-3/70 [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }} text-ink-2">You're the product</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Your members and their data are what's actually being sold. The space works for the platform, not for you.</span></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

        {# owned — flame, the promise #}
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-flame/30 bg-[linear-gradient(160deg,rgba(245,195,68,.08),rgba(255,223,130,.03))] px-[26px] py-7">
          <span class="font-smono text-[.68rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-flame">A space you own</span>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[18px] mt-[18px]">
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-flame [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }}">It looks like you</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Your identity, your structure, your language throughout. Recognisable as yours, and nowhere else's.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-flame [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }}">You set the terms</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Governance, boundaries and moderation are yours to decide, and yours to change whenever your community changes.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-flame [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }}">No one can take it away</b><span class="{{ libt }}">Open source, forkable, exportable. Move it to another team or run it yourself. Walk out with everything, any time.</span></div></div>
            <div class="{{ liw }}"><span class="w-2 h-2 mt-[7px] flex-none bg-flame [clip-path:polygon(50%_0,100%_50%,50%_100%,0_50%)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><div><b class="{{ libh }}">It belongs to your community</b><span class="{{ libt }}">No one's harvesting your members. The space works for the people in it. Full stop.</span></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== what "yours" actually means — value cards ===== #}
    <section class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">What "yours" actually means</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[24ch]">Not a place you rent. <span class="font-light">A place that's built to be yours.</span></h2>

      {% set vcard = "card group rounded-xl border border-ink/15 bg-gradient-to-b from-night-2 to-night px-[26px] py-7 flex flex-col gap-3 hover:border-[color-mix(in_srgb,var(--acc)_40%,transparent)]" %}
      {% set vico = "text-[1.7rem] leading-none text-[var(--acc)]" %}
      {% set vh = "font-disp font-[620] text-[1.18rem] leading-[1.14]" %}
      {% set vt = "text-ink-2 text-[.95rem] m-0" %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[681px]:grid-cols-2 gap-4 mt-[30px]">
        <div class="{{ vcard }}" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
          <i class="ph-duotone ph-fingerprint {{ vico }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3 class="{{ vh }}">Shaped around your community</h3>
          <p class="{{ vt }}">We start from how you already gather (your roles, rituals and rules) and build the space to match. It looks and works like nowhere else, because it's made for one community: yours.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ vcard }}" style="--acc:var(--color-flame)">
          <i class="ph-duotone ph-key {{ vico }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3 class="{{ vh }}">Owned outright, not rented</h3>
          <p class="{{ vt }}">Open source and yours to keep. Forkable, exportable, no per-seat trap, and no subscription you're locked into. Take it to another team or run it yourself whenever you decide.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ vcard }}" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
          <i class="ph-duotone ph-browsers {{ vico }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3 class="{{ vh }}">Your site and your community, one thing</h3>
          <p class="{{ vt }}">The public face and the conversation on the same system, in the same identity. Members move between them without noticing a seam.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ vcard }}" style="--acc:var(--color-corn)">
          <i class="ph-duotone ph-share-network {{ vico }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
          <h3 class="{{ vh }}">Connected on your own terms</h3>
          <p class="{{ vt }}">Federated with the wider open social web, so your members can reach the world, but only as much as you choose. Open the doors wide, or keep it private and invite-only.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== how we build it with you ===== #}
    <section id="how" class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-corn">How we build it with you</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[24ch]">You know your community. <span class="font-light">We know the software.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">Mosaic is those two things in a room together. You make the calls about how your community should run; we work out what that means in software, and everything we build goes back into the commons.</p>

      {% set stepn = "font-smono text-[.75rem] text-flame tracking-[.08em]" %}
      {% set steph = "font-disp font-[620] text-[1.25rem]" %}
      {% set stepw = "font-smono text-[.68rem] text-ink-3 mt-2" %}
      {% set stepp = "text-ink-2 text-[.97rem] m-0 col-start-2 min-[821px]:col-start-auto" %}
      {% set steprow = "grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] min-[821px]:grid-cols-[auto_1fr_1fr] gap-4 min-[821px]:gap-7 items-baseline px-1 py-[26px] border-b border-ink/15" %}
      <div class="mt-7 ">
        <div class="{{ steprow }}">
          <span class="{{ stepn }}">01</span>
          <div><h3 class="{{ steph }}">You talk, we listen</h3></div>
          <p class="{{ stepp }}">Interviews and workshops with your people. How do you gather? Who decides what? Where does it break down today? We've never yet found a community that works the way its org chart says.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ steprow }}">
          <span class="{{ stepn }}">02</span>
          <div><h3 class="{{ steph }}">We co-design it together</h3></div>
          <p class="{{ stepp }}">Together we shape the space: the circles, the roles, the boundaries, the flows. You make the calls about how your community should run; we work out what that means in software.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ steprow }}">
          <span class="{{ stepn }}">03</span>
          <div><h3 class="{{ steph }}">We build it</h3></div>
          <p class="{{ stepp }}">When possible this is simply assembling building blocks that already exist, and that doesn't stop at Bonfire's own extensions. Rather than succumb to "not invented here" syndrome, we interconnect with dedicated open-source tools across the wider ecosystem. We only write new code where something doesn't exist yet, and when we do, it becomes a block anyone can reuse.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ steprow }}">
          <span class="{{ stepn }}">04</span>
          <div><h3 class="{{ steph }}">You take the keys</h3></div>
          <p class="{{ stepp }}">Your brand, your language, your governance, and training for the people who'll actually run it day to day: your facilitators and your moderators. It's yours from here.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ steprow }} !border-b-0">
          <span class="{{ stepn }}">05</span>
          <div><h3 class="{{ steph }}">We watch it grow</h3></div>
          <p class="{{ stepp }}">We get you set up on our cooperative hosting network, or help your team with installing it up on your own infrastructure. And we remain available for updates, fixes and new features.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== proof ===== #}
    <section id="built" class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame">Who we've built with</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[24ch]">Three communities. <span class="font-light">Three different spaces.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">The same foundation, shaped three ways: a magazine, a research network and a care coalition need almost nothing in common. Each one owns what we built together.</p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[821px]:grid-cols-3 gap-[18px] mt-[26px]">
        <a class="card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15 hover:border-ink/25" href="/case-studies/jacobin/">
          <div class="aspect-video border-b border-ink/15 overflow-hidden bg-night-3"><img class="w-full h-full object-cover" src="/img/jacobin/jacobin-social.png" alt="Jacobin's community space on Bonfire" loading="lazy"></div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[9px] flex-1 px-5 py-[22px]">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-flame">A magazine</span>
            <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.18rem] leading-[1.12]">From audience to community</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.93rem] m-0">A community of readers who debate and belong. Publishing stayed on their Ghost site; the community lives on Bonfire, wearing their brand.</p>
            <div class="mt-auto pt-[13px] border-t border-ink/[0.07] font-smono text-[.72rem] text-ink-3 flex justify-between gap-2">span class="text-spark">Read →</span></div>
          </div>
        </a>
        <a class="card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15 hover:border-ink/25" href="https://openscience.network" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
          <div class="aspect-video border-b border-ink/15 overflow-hidden bg-night-3"><img class="w-full h-full object-cover" src="/img/osn22.png" alt="The Open Science Network on Bonfire" loading="lazy"></div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[9px] flex-1 px-5 py-[22px]">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-flame">A research network</span>
            <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.18rem] leading-[1.12]">A commons for scholars</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.93rem] m-0">Co-designed with working researchers: ORCID sign-in, publications on your profile, papers that unfold with their DOI.</p>
            <div class="mt-auto pt-[13px] border-t border-ink/[0.07] font-smono text-[.72rem] text-ink-3 flex justify-between gap-2"><b class="text-ink font-normal">Built with academics</b><span class="text-spark">Visit →</span></div>
          </div>
        </a>
        <div class="card rounded-xl overflow-hidden border border-ink/15">
          <div class="aspect-video border-b border-ink/15 overflow-hidden bg-night-3"><img class="w-full h-full object-cover" src="/img/archi.png" alt="Mentaal, a private federated mental-health network using Archipelago mode" loading="lazy"></div>
          <div class="flex flex-col gap-[9px] flex-1 px-5 py-[22px]">
            <span class="font-smono text-[.66rem] tracking-[.12em] uppercase text-flame">A mental-health network</span>
            <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.18rem] leading-[1.12]">A safe space that's theirs</h3>
            <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.93rem] m-0">Private, invite-only, carefully moderated. Safety and governance designed in from the first workshop.</p>
            <div class="mt-auto pt-[13px] border-t border-ink/[0.07] font-smono text-[.72rem] text-ink-3 flex justify-between gap-2"><b class="text-ink font-normal">500+ members</b><span class="text-spark">Planned</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== commons dividend ===== #}
    <section id="commons" class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-spark">The part no agency can offer</p>
      <div class="rounded-xl border border-spark/35 bg-spark/[0.04] px-8 py-[34px] mt-[26px]">
        <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-2xl mb-3">What you fund, everyone inherits. What others funded, you get for free.</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 text-[1.02rem] max-w-[46rem] m-0">Everything built in Mosaic is open source and goes back into the commons. That changes the economics. Your budget builds shared building blocks that every community draws on, and your own space grows out of it.</p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[761px]:grid-cols-2 gap-[18px] min-[761px]:gap-7 mt-6">
          <div class="border-l-2 border-spark pl-[18px]">
            <b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[5px]">You inherit what others already paid for</b>
            <span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">Researchers funded ORCID sign-in and publication imports. Jacobin funded federated comments and CMS integration. Both are sitting there, free, if you want them. You start further along than they did.</span>
          </div>
          <div class="border-l-2 border-spark pl-[18px]">
            <b class="font-disp font-semibold block mb-[5px]">What you fund outlives you</b>
            <span class="text-ink-2 text-[.95rem]">The block we build for your need becomes available to every community after you. Your budget doesn't just give you a space of your own, but grows the commons everyone builds on.</span>
          </div>
        </div>
        {# <p class="font-disp font-normal text-[1.25rem] mt-[26px] text-ink">"You're not buying software. You're funding a commons, and getting a space of your own out of it."</p> #}
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== ways to work together ===== #}
    <section id="packages" class="py-16 border-t border-ink/[0.07] scroll-mt-[70px]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-corn-2">Ways to work together</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} max-w-[22ch]">However far you want to go, <span class="font-light">you end up owning it.</span></h2>
      <p class="{{ bodyp }}">Every route is bespoke. We don't do per-seat plans or off-the-shelf tiers. Where you land depends on how much your community needs shaped.</p>

      {% set pkg = "card rounded-xl border border-ink/15 px-6 py-[26px] gap-[9px] flex flex-col" %}
      {% set pkgwho = "font-smono text-[.66rem] tracking-[.1em] uppercase text-corn" %}
      {% set pkgfit = "mt-auto pt-3.5 font-smono text-[.7rem] text-ink-3 border-t border-ink/[0.07]" %}
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 min-[901px]:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mt-[26px]">
        <div class="{{ pkg }}">
          <span class="{{ pkgwho }}">You need it to fit</span>
          <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.25rem] mt-1">Tailored space</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.94rem] m-0">Bonfire wearing your identity, with your governance and the integrations you already rely on.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc mt-2 pl-[18px] text-ink-2 text-[.9rem] [&_li]:mb-1"><li>Workshops with your team</li><li>Custom identity, roles &amp; boundaries</li><li>Integrations (CMS, membership, SSO)</li><li>Training + hosting</li></ul>
          <div class="{{ pkgfit }}">◼ Weeks · scoped to a fixed quote</div>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ pkg }}">
          <span class="{{ pkgwho }}">You need something new</span>
          <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.25rem] mt-1">Co-design partnership</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.94rem] m-0">Your community needs capabilities nobody's built yet, the way researchers needed DOIs on their profiles.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc mt-2 pl-[18px] text-ink-2 text-[.9rem] [&_li]:mb-1"><li>Community research &amp; co-design</li><li>New blocks, built with you</li><li>Contributed back to the commons</li><li>Often grant-funded, and we'll help you apply</li></ul>
          <div class="{{ pkgfit }}">◼ Months · scoped together</div>
        </div>
        <div class="{{ pkg }}">
          <span class="{{ pkgwho }}">You want us to stay</span>
          <h3 class="font-disp font-[620] text-[1.25rem] mt-1">Ongoing partnership</h3>
          <p class="text-ink-2 text-[.94rem] m-0">The unglamorous part that keeps a space alive: we maintain the code, a co-op runs the infrastructure.</p>
          <ul class="list-disc mt-2 pl-[18px] text-ink-2 text-[.9rem] [&_li]:mb-1"><li>Code updates &amp; new features, on a retainer</li><li>Hosting &amp; backups via our co-op network</li><li>A human to call when it breaks</li><li>Or a clean handover, whenever you want</li></ul>
          <div class="{{ pkgfit }}">◼ Ongoing · a retainer, cancel anytime and keep your space</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-xl border border-dashed border-ink/15 px-[26px] py-6 mt-[22px]">
        <p class="m-0 text-ink-2 text-base"><b class="text-ink font-semibold">Tell us your budget and we'll tell you honestly what's possible</b>, including when the answer is "you don't need us, here's how to do it yourself." And if self-hosting is the right call, we can still help you get there through community <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="/self-hosting#guided">install parties or a 1-on-1 setup session</a>. We'd rather send you away with a working plan than take money for a project that shouldn't happen.</p>
      </div>
    </div></section>

    {# ===== final ===== #}
    <section id="talk" class="py-20 text-center border-t border-ink/[0.07]">
    <div class="max-w-[1180px] mx-auto px-7">
      <p class="{{ eyebrow }} text-flame justify-center">Let's talk</p>
      <h2 class="{{ display }} mx-auto max-w-[20ch]">Tell us how your community works.</h2>
      <p class="mx-auto mt-3.5 text-[1.02rem] text-ink-2 max-w-[46ch]">We take on only a handful of communities a year, and we start by listening. If it's a fit, you walk away owning something no one can take from you.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-3 mt-[26px]">
        <a class="{{ btnfire }}" href="https://cal.com/bonfire-networks/meet">Book a call</a>
        <a class="{{ btnline }}" href="#built">See what we've built</a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 font-smono text-[.8rem] text-ink-3">or email <a class="text-spark hover:underline" href="mailto:mosaic@bonfirenetworks.org">mosaic@bonfirenetworks.org</a></p>
    </div></section>

  </div>
</div>
